                <pb facs="0667" n="582" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg582"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.61383/175: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-16T12:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">November 16,
                                1919, noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 7.26
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3277. Jenkins telegraphs that he was released without bail after two hours
                    detention in penitentiary and is now restricted to his home. In a signed
                    statement published in local press today prosecuting attorney [of] Puebla says
                    Jenkins is guilty of criminal responsibility and giving false evidence and has
                    been transferred to his home to avoid recurrence of recent illness.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
